OBJECTIVE OF THE ENGAGEMENT
The overall objective of the engagement is to undertake a capacity building program in test development and marking of promotional examinations administered by the Public Service Commission including:
The Proficiency Examination for Clerical Officers;
The Administrative Officers’ Examination;
The Assistant Legal Metrology Officers Examination Parts I& II.
Details Terms of Reference and other terms of engagement will be provided to successful applicants.
MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS FOR ENGAGEMENT AS AN EXAMINER
Applicants will be required to meet the following minimum requirements:
Academic and Professional Qualifications:
A Bachelor’s degree or its equivalent in the relevant subject area;
Professional Qualification in relevant subject areas of interest where applicable;
Work Experience
At least six years’ experience in professional practice, research or training;
Evidence of having worked as a contracted professional in other examination bodies will be an added advantage.
Other requirements that successful candidates will be expected to demonstrate include:
Must meet the requirements of Chapter Six of the Constitution on leadership and integrity;
Ability to work within strict timelines as shall be specified by the Commission; and
Ability to maintain security, confidentiality and integrity of the examination process on engagement.
go to method of application »

Company Details:
The Commission dates back to 1954 when Civil Service Commission was established by British Colonial Government following Holmes Commission Report, 1948;
Civil Service Commission was advisory to the Governor in matters of appointments;
At independence in 1963 it was enshrined in the constitution an...read mored renamed Public Service Commission;
Independence Constitution had Regional PSC’s but abolished in 1964 following constitutional amendments;
It is the oldest Constitutional Commission and its mandate has expanded over the years.
The Commission then constituted of a chairman, a deputy chairman and fifteen members all appointed by the President.
The Commission, since then, has handled matters of human resource management in the public service especially the civil service and local authorities.
Constitution of Kenya, 2010 promulgated on 27th August 2010 reconstituted the Commission with a redefined and expanded mandate and a lean membership.

