Be visionary and be able establish effective plans that take into consideration long-term aspects;
Be able to make decisions, as well as willing to take responsibility for his or decisions when under pressure;
Leading people as well as coordinating people and resources;
Be able to embrace change;
Effective in managing productivity;
Ability to uphold standards within the organisation ensuring that high quality products and services are provided as well as ensuring that trust is created and maintained;
Demonstrable competency in resolving conflicts in the workplace;
Be able to empower others including encouraging others, motivating as well as inspiring others;
Have ability to facilitate or catalyse change in an organisation;
Be able to provide due consideration to risks, rewards and the cost of control measures in evaluating business opportunities, process and system changes;
Have ability to translate the organisation's vision and long term goals into medium and short term deliverables;
Have knowledge and understanding of costing, budgeting and finance concepts and the understanding and application of related processes and procedures;
Have ability to identify and capitalise on opportunities and manage risks; and
Be able to create mechanisms to ensure that designed processes are implemented correctly and that process changes are made thoughtfully, taking into consideration the impacts on people, other processes and technology.

